{
  "description": "Page Jira's list operations (https://developer.atlassian.com/cloud/jira/platform/rest/v3/intro/#pagination); the spec marks none. `startAt` lists take `startAt`/`maxResults` and return `startAt`, `maxResults`, `total` and, on `PageBean` lists, `isLast` beside the items (`values`, or `comments`, `worklogs`, `dashboards`, `issueTypes` on the older beans); src/pagination.ts advances `startAt` by the items received and stops on `isLast`, `total` or an empty page. `mode: token` lists take `nextPageToken` and return `nextPageToken`, absent on the last page (JQL search, bulk changelogs, invalid-JQL audit entries, and the status/workflow usage pages, which nest it with their `values`), or take `cursor` and return `nextPageCursor` (plans, plan teams, policies; `startAt` is 'legacy' on policies and 'only 0 is accepted in cursor mode'). All read off the spec's own parameter and response schemas. Left out: operations that return a bare array (user searches) and `getCreateIssueMetaIssueTypeId`, whose page bean has two item arrays (`fields`, `results`).",
